  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Internews media programme Zimbabwe</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Internews mediaprogram Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Internews Europe har ans&#xf6;kt om programst&#xf6;d p&#xe5; 22 miljoner SEK f&#xf6;r sitt program &quot;Zimbabwe Media Development&quot; under 2019-2021. Programmet kommer fr&#xe4;mst att verka i s&#xf6;dra Zimbabwe, men kommer &#xe4;ven att ha ett antal aktiviteter i Harare (i sammarbete med det medieprogram som drivs av Fojo, vilket fr&#xe4;mst fokuserar p&#xe5; norra delarna av Zimbabwe). 

&quot;Zimbabwe Media Development&quot; &#xe4;r designat f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka och kapacitetsutveckla den oberoende mediesektorn samt civilsamh&#xe4;llet i landet, d&#xe4;r stort fokus ligger p&#xe5; att utveckla anv&#xe4;ndandet av digital media, f&#xf6;r att man ska kunna framst&#xe4;lla och n&#xe5; ut till befolkningen med opartisk information som fr&#xe4;mjar inkludering och ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande. M&#xe5;lgruppen f&#xf6;r programmet &#xe4;r fr&#xe4;mst kvinnor och unga.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Internews Europe has applied for programme support of 22 million SEK for their &quot;Zimbabwe Media Developement&quot; (ZMD) programme during 2019 - 2021. The ZMD programme will primarily focus its work on Southern Zimbabwe (Bulawayo, Matabeleland North, Matabeleland South and Midlands). Some activities will also be in Harare (in cooperation with the media programme by Fojo which will focus on the Northern parts of the country). 

The programme is designed to ensure a resilient, digitally-enabled and sustainable independent media and civil society in Southern Zimbabwe to have the skills, knowledge and tools they need to reach citizens with accurate and impartial information that promotes inclusion and accountability. The target group for the programme are mainly women and youth.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention is expected to increase the quantity and reach of independent, reliable and data-driven information into the public sphere, with a focus on content production and consumption by women, youth and rural communities. Further it is expected to strengthen the capacity of media and civil society to inform and elevate citizen voices as key to holding the government accountable on key project themes i.e. governance, human rights, gender, corruption, health, environment, climate change.

 Finally, the ZMD programme is expected to improve the business and financial sustainability of independent media.</narrative>
  </description>
